223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-10T21:27:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-10T21:27:34Z","body":"> I was thinking we may want a way to manage these directly in the find in files dialog. And then it could be saved as metadata instead of a setting.\r\n\r\nThe only advantage is that it makes configuration more discoverable (right now it's not mentioned anywhere in the dialog, while #110388 adds it to the tooltip). It'd require UX design changes and needs a proposal, which may take a while, so I think this PR is fine in the meantime.\r\n\r\n> Or maybe even remove them like suggested here https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/14027#discussioncomment-16008302 (and the default Includes field could be the default extensions)\r\n\r\nYou mean remove the setting, or the checkboxes? Filtering by extensions is convenient, because it allows to limit the amount of searched files a lot (and searching is very slow). Multiple projects are likely to use the same filters, so it's better to store it globally too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues